    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0954" n="834" xml:id="pg834"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-10T18:00:00+01:00">October 10, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 10—2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>294. Department’s 152, October 7, 7 p.m. After explaining situation to Avenol
                    today he assured me that name “Monetary and Economic Conference” would
                    immediately be resumed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
